HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The rroouuttee command appeared in 4.2BSD.  IPv6 support was added by
     WIDE/KAME project.

     The --rreeccvvppiippee, --hhooppccoouunntt, --sseennddppiippee, --sssstthhrreesshh, --rrtttt, and --rrttttvvaarr modi‐
     fiers used to be used to initialize various quantities in routing table
     entries.  The routing system no longer uses these values and the modi‐
     fiers exist now only for compatibility with other operating systems.

BBUUGGSS
     Some uses of the --iiffaa or --iiffpp modifiers with the aadddd command will incor‐
     rectly fail with a “Network is unreachable” message if there is no de‐
     fault route.  See case RTM_ADD in rroouuttee__oouuttppuutt() from _s_y_s_/_n_e_t_/_r_t_s_o_c_k_._c
     for details.

